__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
# `env/` unanchored also swallowed studio/packages/ui/src/env/ — 10 real source files,
# which made a fresh clone fail to typecheck. Anchor it: a stray root-level virtualenv is
# ignored, nested `.venv`/`venv` are covered above, and source dirs named `env` are safe.
/env/
node_modules/
dist/
build/
# electron-builder's buildResources (icons, entitlements, the afterPack + notarize hooks)
# live in a dir literally named `build/`. Without these a packaged app has no icon, no
# entitlements, and no exec bit on the node-pty spawn-helper ("No terminal backend").
!studio/apps/desktop/build/
out/
.next/
.turbo/
.cache/
.parcel-cache/
coverage/
*.so
*.log
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.DS_Store
.idea/

# scan reports go stale and are regenerated by scripts/secret-scan.sh — the CONFIG
# (.gitleaks.toml) is the durable artifact, not the output.
/.security/

# --- internal working documents: never in the published repo ------------------
# Plans, audits and diagnostic reports are notes to ourselves. They name internal
# paths, unfixed defects and release timing — useful here, a liability in public.
# Root-anchored so product docs (README.md, studio/*/README.md, PRIVACY.md,
# python/sidecar/CONTRACT.md) are untouched. New working notes: name them
# `<TOPIC>-PLAN.md` / `<TOPIC>-REPORT.md` / `<TOPIC>-AUDIT.md` at the root, or drop
# them in /notes/, and they stay out automatically.
/*-PLAN.md
/*-REPORT.md
/*-AUDIT.md
/*-NOTES.md
# `FIXES-<dates>.md` matched NONE of the suffix patterns above, so it was committed by
# default — and it carried `/Users/<name>/ALPHA/PROMETHEUS` on line 4, the only personal-path
# leak in the whole tree (found 2026-09-26 by scripts/check-personal-data.sh). A note is a note
# whichever end of the name says so, so the PREFIX forms are ignored too.
/FIXES-*.md

# Scratch API responses saved while poking at an endpoint, and then committed by the
# auto-committer, which runs `git add -A` and cannot tell a probe from a fixture.
# Found 2026-09-30: studio/ held `nd.json` (nodejs.org's release index, 26k lines),
# `eol.json` (endoflife.date), `py.json` (python releases), `ov.json` (`{"version":"0.34.1"}`)
# and `u.json` (one ollama download URL) — five files, tracked, referenced by NOTHING, and
# destined for a public repo. `studio/pyruntime.lock.json` is the real one and stays.
#
# Anchored to the two directories where the probing happens, so a package.json, tsconfig or
# any legitimately-named config elsewhere is untouched. If you are saving a response to look
# at, give it one of these names and it can never be committed by accident:
/scratch-*.json
/*.probe.json
/studio/scratch-*.json
/studio/*.probe.json
/FIXES/
/HANDOFF*.md
/*-HANDOFF.md
/*-FIXES.md
/*-SUMMARY.md
/*-STATUS.md
/DEPLOYMENT-PLAN.md
/SLASH-COMMANDS-REPORT.md
/notes/
/all_wrongs_*.md
# Design/GUI-redesign handoff notes: internal reasoning, exact token values, and (in the
# bundled reference-prototype.html mockups) placeholder demo data that has named other,
# unrelated private projects. Never in the published repo — mirrored to ALPHA_local_only
# instead of deleted, since the content itself has ongoing value as design reference.
/handoff*/
studio/notes.txt
# NOT ignored, deliberately: THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md. It is a redistribution
# obligation under Apache-2.0 §4(d) and the PSF license of the bundled CPython —
# it must ship WITH the code, not be stripped from it.

# working notes / debug leftovers that have no business in a public repo
curl.trace
resume.txt

# runtime session logs from running/testing the desktop app locally — regenerated on
# every run, not source; a real `.prometheus/` PROJECT config (settings.json, command/,
# agents/) would be a deliberate, separate thing this rule does not need to hide since
# none exists in this repo today.
studio/**/.prometheus/

# Claude Code runtime state (never commit)
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/*.lock

# --- local-only (kept on disk, never in remote) ---
/MDS/
/AI_SKILLS_WONDERLAND/
.claude/
.cursor/
.windsurf/
.clinerules/
.opencode/
.junie/
.agents/
/docs/plan/
/docs/interface/

# 2-second RAM trace written by handoffs/ram-2sec-log.sh — machine-local evidence,
# regenerated per session, never published.
/2_sec_ram_log.md

# Backup files that reached the index because nothing matched them, found in the
# pre-publication audit 2026-09-30.
#
# The case that got through was `CLAUDE.md.bak-<timestamp>`: an editor/agent backup of the
# working-instructions file, carrying a SUPERSEDED copy of rules that are load-bearing
# (CLAUDE.md §4: "Comments in this repo are load-bearing"), so a reader could have followed the
# stale one believing it current. The timestamp suffix defeated every suffix rule already here —
# the same way `FIXES-<dates>.md` did above.
#
# Agent-generated scratch at the repo root is the other half of this problem. A test fixture that
# prompts "write <name>.py" produces a real file, and the auto-committer (`git add -A`) cannot
# tell it from a fixture. There is no pattern that catches an arbitrary generated filename, so the
# defence is the pre-publication audit: check the ROOT LISTING (`git ls-files | grep -v /`) before
# publishing, and keep it to files a visitor should see.
*.bak
*.bak-*
/CLAUDE.md.bak*

# --- agent working instructions + vendor docs: local-only, never published -----
#
# CLAUDE.md is the working-instructions file for AI agents operating IN this checkout. It is not
# product documentation: it carries one machine's incident forensics (kernel lockup counts, dates,
# process tallies), and it points at `handoffs/` scripts that `/handoff*/` above deliberately
# withholds from the repo. A public clone would get instructions referencing files it does not
# have. Untracked rather than deleted — it still governs work in this checkout.
/CLAUDE.md
/PROMETHEUS.md
/AGENTS.md
#
# `studio/auth.md` was a verbatim copy of LM STUDIO's own documentation, MDX `<Callout>` tags and
# all. Redistributing another project's docs from a repo that ships a THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md is a
# licensing question nobody needs; it was moved to ALPHA_local_only.
/studio/auth.md
#
# Planning and audit notes generated while building (the `-PLAN`/`-REPORT` patterns above already
# cover the common shapes). Moved to ~/ALPHA_local_only/PROMETHEUS/ on 2026-09-30.
/*-SURVEY*.md
